Confirmed: flutter_test's `testWidgets` takes `bool? skip` — no reason string. So for the 3 golden scenarios: use `skip: true` and carry the full documented reason in the comment block above each scenario (which I already wrote). To keep the reason greppable at the skip site, use `skip: _pendingRebake` with a documented file-level constant:

```dart
/// gh-2004: these scenarios' committed baselines are stale ... The list
/// doubles as the unskip checklist.
const _pendingRebake = true;
``

Hmm — a constant set to `true` looks odd. Better: `skip: _baselineRebakePending` where `_baselineRebakePending = true` with the doc comment explaining. When the re-bake lands, flip to false or remove. Actually simplest honest: `skip: true` + comments. But a named constant at file scope with the full story, referenced by all 3 skips in BOTH files? Cross-file sharing → put it in golden_test_helper.dart? There's precedent of `skip: !_enabled` patterns.

Decision: in each of the two test files, a file-level const:

```dart
/// gh-2004: baselines for the gema-affected scenarios are stale (the
/// widget surface changed) and may only be re-baked on the pinned macOS
/// release runner (memory n_1018_80a7 — a linux re-bake corrupts them).
/// Skips stay until that re-bake lands; unskip in the same change as the
/// `flutter test/golden --update-goldens` re-bake of the named
/// golden files.
const _goldenRebakePending = true;
``

and use `skip: _goldenRebakePending`. Keep my comment blocks (shortened where duplicative).

Note: package:test's plain `test()` DOES accept String skip — but testWidgets doesn't. Fix the two files.

